Threading

        Threads share the same memory.

        Best for:

        API calls
        Waiting tasks
        Network requests
        File IO
        Database operations

        Example:

        Listening to multiple stock feeds simultaneously
Multiprocessing

        Processes have separate memory.

        Best for:

        Heavy calculations
        ML models
        Backtesting
        Monte Carlo
        Risk calculations

        Example:

        Calculating VaR on 10 years of data

Golden Rule
        Use Case	Best Tool
        Waiting on network/file/db	Threading
        Heavy CPU math	Multiprocessing
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

put() → assign task
get() → employee picks task
task_done() → employee reports completion
join() → manager waits until all reports are complete

Without task_done(), manager keeps waiting.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

what is generator function?

A generator function is a special type of function in Python that allows you to create an iterator.
Instead of returning a single value, a generator function uses the `yield` keyword to produce
a sequence of values over time, one at a time. This makes it memory efficient, as it generates
values on the fly rather than storing them all in memory at once.

def numbers():
    yield 1
    yield 2
    yield 3

g = numbers()

print(next(g))
print(next(g))
print(next(g))


